
========================================================================
OCTOMAP — the load that actually scales with sweep rate
========================================================================
  Private /bench octomap_server fed REAL /scan_raw geometry,
  re-pitched through the sweep range so the raycasts are as long
  and as varied as a real sweep.  The live octomap is untouched.

  captured 12 real scans (2801 beams each)
  bank: 12 clouds, 2184 points mean, pitched -45..+45 deg
  raycast work per cloud ~ 2184 pts x 80 voxels = 0.17 M traversals
  bench octomap pid [4525]

  pub Hz           sent   inserted   keep up?  oct %core
  7.2               6.7        6.7       100%       36.9

  "keep up?" below ~95%% means octomap_server is dropping clouds: it is
  single-threaded, so the message filter backs up and you get the
  "queue is full" symptom rather than an error.
